# Baseline: meizu_m6_defconfig (same MT6755 SoC, same PMIC/clk/pll/spm
# topology). Deltas for M6T hardware are signalled with "M6T" comments and are
# each backed by kallsyms/DTS evidence:
#   - AKM09911 magnetometer  (kallsyms akm09911_* / DTS msensor@0f)
#   - Goodix GF3258 FP        (kallsyms GF3258_GOODIX strings)
#   - Dual rear camera (DTS camera_main@1a + camera_main2@36 + camera_sub@2d
#     + camera_main_af@0c) -> IMGSENSOR list from stock kallsyms probe names
#   - 720x1440 18:9 panel (DTS atag,videolfb-lcmname=ili9881c_hd_dsi_txd)
#   - Project ID = meizu_m6t + appended DTB image name = meizu_m6t
#
# KNOWN GAPS requiring further RE (see KERNEL_REVERSE_HANDOFF.md §Stop cues):
#   - No source-side LCM driver matches the M6T atag "ili9881c_hd_dsi_txd"
#     exactly; the stock kernel instead compiles ft8613/hx83102b/nt36525 panel
#     drivers (multivendor) which are NOT in the M6 source tree. We select the
#     closest available ili9881c source variant (ili9881c_hd720_dsi_vdo_dijing)
#     so the build wires correctly; the panel almost certainly will NOT init
#     until the right init sequence is RE-ported from stock vmlinux.
#   - AW869X haptic amplifier (i2c@5a in stock DTS) driver is NOT in source;
#     kept CONFIG_MTK_VIBRATOR=y so the framework wires up — vibration effect
#     quality will differ until aw869x is ported.
